e history-writing project, although new to Yemen, bore some resemblance to a far better known scholarly enterprise of the new Turkish Republic.1 These collateral maʿarif efforts were further assertions of a tentative yet determined attitude toward developing the state\'s identity and extending its authority by means of new textual technologies.\'  It is assumed here that historiography was produced during the Ottoman period as well.'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 878, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 776})
